In MongoDB, we don't need to explicitly create a collection. A collection will be automatically created when a document is inserted into it. Therefore, we can't explicitly define the fields during creation of a collection similar to creating tables in SQL.

However, we can insert some sample data with the fields you mentioned to implicitly create this collection. Here is a MongoDB query to insert a document into an "orders" collection:

```javascript
db.orders.insert({
    "order_id": "001",
    "customer_id": "C001",
    "total_amount": 250.99,
    "payment_status": "paid",
    "delivery_status": "delivered"
})
```

This code will create a new document in the "orders" collection with fields: order_id, customer_id, total_amount, payment_status and delivery_status. If the "orders" collection does not already exist, it will be created. 

If you want to enforce a schema (specific structure of the documents), you will have to use MongoDB's Data Modeling and Schema Validation, which allows you to specify the structure of the documents in a collection. This feature is available from MongoDB version 3.6 and above.

Here is an example of how you can defined a schema:

```javascript
db.createCollection("orders", {
   validator: {
      $jsonSchema: {
         bsonType: "object",
         required: [ "order_id", "customer_id", "total_amount", "payment_status", "delivery_status" ],
         properties: {
            order_id: {
               bsonType: "string",
               description: "must be a string and is required"
            },
            customer_id: {
               bsonType: "string",
               description: "must be a string and is required"
            },
            total_amount: {
               bsonType: [ "double" ],
               description: "must be a double and is required"
            },
            payment_status: {
               bsonType: "string",
               description: "must be a string and is required"
            },
            delivery_status: {
               bsonType: "string",
               description: "must be a string and is required"
            }
         }
      }
   }
})
```

Keep in mind the validation rules are not retroactive but will apply to any new documents inserted or any existing document updated in the orders collection.

