```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(fibonacciSequence(10));
    }

    public static String fibonacciSequence(int n) {
        // handle edge cases
        if (n < 1 || n > 50) {
            return "Invalid input. Please, provide a positive integer less than or equal to 50.";
        }

        // declare an array to store the Fibonacci sequence
        long[] sequence = new long[n];

        // calculate the first 'n' terms of the Fibonacci sequence
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (i == 0) {
                sequence[i] = 0;
            } else if (i == 1) {
                sequence[i] = 1;
            } else {
                sequence[i] = sequence[i - 1] + sequence[i - 2];
            }
        }

        // create a string representation of the sequence
        StringBuilder sequenceStr = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (i > 0) {
                sequenceStr.append(", ");
            }
            sequenceStr.append(sequence[i]);
        }

        return sequenceStr.toString();
    }
}
```

This program creates a string representation of the first 'n' Fibonacci numbers. If 'n' is less than 1 or greater than 50, it returns an error message. The calculation is done using a simple loop and the results are stored in an array. The elements of the array are then combined into a string using StringBuilder for output.

