Here's how this can be dealt using Java.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] nums = {-2,1,-3,4,-1,2,1,-5,4};

        System.out.println(maxSubArray(nums));
    }

    public static int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        int maxSoFar = nums[0];
        int maxEndingHere = nums[0];

        for(int i  = 1; i < nums.length; i++){
            maxEndingHere = Math.max(maxEndingHere + nums[i], nums[i]);
            maxSoFar = Math.max(maxSoFar, maxEndingHere);
        }
        return maxSoFar;
    }
}
```
This algorithm works by initializing two variables, `maxSoFar` and `maxEndingHere`, to the first element of the array. Then, it iterates over each element in the array, updating `maxEndingHere` to be the maximum of `maxEndingHere + nums[i]` and `nums[i]`, and `maxSoFar` to be the maximum of `maxSoFar` and `maxEndingHere`. Finally, it returns `maxSoFar`, which holds the maximum subsequence sum.

