The Site.DesignMode property works for nested controls, unlike the DesignMode property. The helper method also considers the LicenseManager.UsageMode, which is correctly set during the initialization of controls at design-time. 

Please be aware that Microsoft has not officially documented the Site.DesignMode property. So use this with caution. 

Anyway, Microsoft has recognized this problem and has created a new property called `DesignerProperties.IsInDesignModeProperty` which works correctly. But it's only available if you're developing with WPF.

As for asking Microsoft to fix it internally, you can voice this on forums that are directly monitored by the Microsoft development team, such as Microsoft's UserVoice or the Visual Studio developer community.

