1. A constructor that takes a C-style string (const char*) as an argument and initializes the internal pointer to point to the same string.
2. A method to return the length of the string.
3. A method to return the character at a specified index in the string.
4. A method to concatenate another string to the current string and return a new string object.

You need to implement the class `SimpleString` with the following private member:
```cpp
