Error handling in workbox can be implemented using the catch handler while registering the routes. This way, if an error occurs during the fetching of resources, your custom error handling logic will be triggered.

Let's say you are routing for JavaScript files.

```javascript
    workbox.routing.registerRoute(
      /\.(?:js)$/,
      new workbox.strategies.NetworkFirst({
        cacheName: 'js-cache',
      }),
      'GET'
    );
```

To add error handling here, modify the routine registration as follows:

```javascript
    workbox.routing.registerRoute(
      /\.(?:js)$/,
      new workbox.strategies.NetworkFirst({
        cacheName: 'js-cache',
      }),
      'GET'
    ).catch((error) => {
      console.error(`Custom error handling: ${error}`);
      //Other custom error handling logic
    });
```

Additionally, for generic error handling you can use:

```javascript
